{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/3477","id":4520049810,"node_id":"PR_kwDOEFLz888AAAABDWp8kg","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3477","diff_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3477.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3477.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/3477","number":3477,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"db: quote postgres connection parameters","user":{"login":"YpNo","id":883643,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4MzY0Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/883643?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YpNo","html_url":"https://github.com/YpNo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YpNo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YpNo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YpNo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YpNo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YpNo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YpNo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YpNo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YpNo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YpNo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The Postgres DSN was assembled by string concatenation:\r\n\r\n    dbString += \" password=\" + cfg.Postgres.Pass\r\n\r\nlibpq's keyword/value format splits on whitespace, so a password containing a\r\nspace was cut off at the space and the remainder parsed as further parameters.\r\nA value with a single quote or backslash broke parsing in similar ways. The\r\nfailure is silent: the connection simply fails to authenticate, or worse, a\r\npassword containing `sslmode=disable` turns TLS off.\r\n\r\nThis moves the DSN into a `postgresDSN` helper that quotes every value with\r\n`pgQuote`, following the libpq rules: wrap in single quotes, escape `\\` and `'`\r\nwith a backslash. Host, database name, user, password and a raw `ssl` value\r\nsuch as `verify-full` all go through it. The `ssl` handling is unchanged:\r\n`true` keeps the libpq default, `false` adds `sslmode=disable`, anything else\r\nis passed through as an `sslmode` value.\r\n\r\nThe startup log line used to print the DSN before the password was appended.\r\nIt now logs the DSN built from a copy of the config with the password cleared,\r\nso the redaction no longer depends on statement order.\r\n\r\n`TestBuildPostgresDSN` covers the three `ssl` forms, a unix-socket host, an\r\nomitted port and password, and a password containing a space, a quote, a\r\nbackslash and an embedded `sslmode=disable`. I also confirmed the quoted output\r\nround-trips through pgx's `pgconn.ParseConfig` with the expected host, port,\r\ndatabase, user and password; that check is not committed to keep pgx an\r\nindirect dependency.\r\n\r\n- [x] have read the CONTRIBUTING.md file\r\n- [ ] raised a GitHub issue or discussed it on the projects chat beforehand\r\n- [x] added unit tests\r\n- [ ] added integration tests\r\n- [ ] updated documentation if needed\r\n- [x] updated CHANGELOG.md","created_at":"2026-09-13T17:53:17Z","updated_at":"2026-09-17T17:22:08Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"nblock","id":131119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMTExOQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131119?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock","html_url":"https://github.com/nblock","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/subscriptions","organizations_url":